@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+I am writing to apply for the Senior Director, Digital Technology Solutions, Enterprise Systems role supporting Enterprise Systems at NeoGenomics. Ramsey is a straightforward drive from where I live in Montville, and the role itself sits close to the center of what I have spent the last several years doing: owning the enterprise application ecosystem for a commercial-stage life sciences company and using it as the platform for automation across Finance, HR, Legal, and Supply Chain, rather than treating those functions as separate technology silos.
+
+At SK Life Science I moved from Enterprise Architect through Head of Applications to Head of IT over roughly seven years, and by the end I owned SAP S/4HANA (FICO/MM) and Ariba lifecycle management alongside UKG and iCIMS for HR, with Workday evaluated as part of a broader HRIS strategy. That progression gave me the vantage point your posting describes: partner to HR, Finance, Legal, and Supply Chain leaders, translating what they needed operationally into a technology roadmap, then holding the vendors and the internal team accountable for delivering it. I reduced operating expenses by 30% through vendor renegotiation, cloud rightsizing, and license consolidation, and I did that while also supporting K-SOX reporting for our Korean parent, with ITGCs designed to US SOX 404 standards, so I understand what compliance discipline this kind of role has to carry alongside the automation agenda.
+
+The automation and AI-first framing in your posting is not new territory for me. I directed AI-enabled automation of first-line security operations that removed a meaningful chunk of manual Level 1 triage work, built an MSL next-best-action model on Snowflake Cortex that applied natural language processing to years of unstructured field notes, and stood up AI-based expense anomaly detection, together worth an estimated $300,000 to $500,000 in annual savings. None of that ran unsupervised in a regulated environment; validated systems remained the system of record, audit trails stayed intact, and people reviewed outputs before anything got acted on. I also led an enterprise-wide RPA vendor evaluation across UiPath, Automation Anywhere, and Blue Prism, so I know the ground your posting is standing on even where my hands-on platform time sits more with the surrounding architecture than with bot development itself.
+
+I have owned ServiceNow as our ITSM platform, built a data governance framework with a COO-chaired council spanning Finance, Legal, HR, IT, and QA, and supported an analytics environment with roughly 150 production dashboards used by around 400 business users across Commercial, Finance, and HR. I have also led technology diligence and Day-1 integration planning across two business combinations, which is the kind of work that tests whether an enterprise systems strategy actually holds up under pressure rather than just on a roadmap slide. I would welcome the chance to talk through how that background applies directly to what NeoGenomics is trying to build in Ramsey.
+
+Thank you for considering my application. I would be glad to discuss the role further at your convenience.